.TH AUDINUX 1 "2026-11-13" "audinux 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audinux \- long-audio player with a multi-line waveform, markers and A\-B loop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audinux
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audinux
is a graphical audio player intended for long recordings: audiobooks,
sermons, lectures and podcasts lasting from a few minutes to several hours.
The whole file is drawn as a multi-line waveform that always fits the
window, so any position can be reached with a single click instead of
scrolling.
.PP
Waveforms are generated in the background while playback starts
immediately, and are cached on disk so that reopening the same file is
fast. If
.B audiowaveform
is installed it is used for generation; otherwise
.B ffmpeg
is used.
.PP
Playback is performed by VLC (libVLC) directly from the original file, so
no re\-encoding takes place and quality is preserved.
.PP
Named markers are stored per audio file. Two markers around the current
position define an A\-B loop.
.SH OPTIONS
The program takes no command line options. If
.I file
is given, it is opened on startup.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Space
Play or pause.
.TP
.B S
Stop playback.
.TP
.B M
Add a marker at the current position.
.TP
.B L
Enable or disable the A\-B loop.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open an audio file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Add audio files to the playlist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Audinux/Audinux.conf
Window layout and last used settings, stored with QSettings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/audinux/markers/
Marker lists, one JSON file per audio file.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/audinux/
Cached waveform data.
.PP
The directories follow the XDG Base Directory specification
.RB ( XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vlc (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
